  "form_alias_note": "form_aliases map common oxide / supported forms back to their dominant element factor. This is a deliberate first-order approximation: the elemental factor is applied per kg of material (so 1 kg of Al2O3 is treated as 1 kg of Al at the cradle-to-gate stage). For high-precision LCA on oxides, prefer the explicit oxide entries above (TiO2, ZrO2). Mixed-metal forms (NiFe-LDH, NiOOH, MoS2) map to their dominant element by mass under the same approximation. A parenthetical qualifier in a name ('TiO2 (anatase)') is ignored for lookup. Items not listed in factors or aliases are treated as 'no_data' and the LCA result flags a data gap.",
